Subject: [PATCH] Keep footprint snapshots alive during background library reload

The library-table dialog starts asynchronous preloading and immediately asks
open editors to rebuild their trees. GetFootprints used to drop its read lock
before returning borrowed pointers; a worker could replace the cache and delete
those objects while the UI was still in FOOTPRINT::GetSearchTerms().

Return shared ownership and retain it in every consumer through the last read.
Notify the editor, viewer and CVPCB after preloading finishes, not when it starts.
Include a deterministic QA regression for a snapshot surviving worker replacement.

Applies after the local KiCad 10.0.8 series (0002 through 0020).

